WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.248
A Java team wants to call the Kotlin event library.

2
00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.155
javac can't read Kotlin.

3
00:00:08.155 --> 00:00:14.907
It reads the class files kotlinc wrote, and some Kotlin features look odd there, or are missing.

4
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:17.639
First, default arguments.

5
00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:20.611
From Kotlin, PlainBus of refunds works.

6
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:24.759
From Java, the same call fails: no suitable constructor found.

7
00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:29.444
The class file has only two: the one with every default, and the full one.

8
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:34.421
@JvmOverloads tells kotlinc to write the ones in between.

9
00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:36.507
Now Java's call compiles.

10
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:40.405
The reified subscribe is invisible to Java.

11
00:00:40.405 --> 00:00:44.905
It's compiled as a synthetic method, and javac ignores those.

12
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:49.257
The KClass one works, if Java converts the class by hand.

13
00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:52.524
The fix: an overload that takes a Java Class.

14
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:59.875
From Java, an object member goes through INSTANCE, and a companion val through Companion and a getter.

15
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.967
@JvmStatic makes publish a real static method.

16
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:07.665
@JvmField makes SYSTEM a plain static field.

17
00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.500
Last, the event.

18
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.673
Its id and amount are value classes, whose init blocks check every value.

19
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.256
In the class file, a value class is just what it wraps.

20
00:01:18.256 --> 00:01:24.236
So Java sees a private constructor that takes a String and a long, and getters with mangled names.

21
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:29.590
A @JvmName shortcut would let Java pass a raw long straight past init.

22
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.712
The facade does the opposite.

23
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:38.129
It takes plain values, and builds the value classes itself, so every init block runs.

24
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.940
A good call goes through.

25
00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.322
Predict.

26
00:01:42.322 --> 00:01:47.350
A Java caller passes 7781, with no pay_ prefix.

27
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.740
What happens?

28
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:54.107
PaymentId's init throws, just as it would for Kotlin.

29
00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:58.204
Here is the facade in Kotlin, and a Java caller.

30
00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:01.326
The rule.

31
00:02:01.326 --> 00:02:03.633
Java sees only the class file.

32
00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:11.171
Give it Class overloads, @JvmOverloads, statics, and a facade that still builds the value classes.

33
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.600
Check yourself.

34
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:19.157
Without @JvmOverloads, does new PlainBus with a name and a flag compile from Java?

35
00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:22.150
Yes.

36
00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.770
The full constructor is always there.

37
00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.391
Only the ones in between are missing.
